statement:
Let $Y$ be a scheme [def-pc-scheme] and $M$ a finite abelian group. An *$M$-torsor over $Y$* is a finite etale [def-weil-pbc-finite-etale-category] surjective [def-weil-surjective-morphism] morphism $\pi:P\to Y$ together with an action $m\mapsto(m+\cdot)$ of $M$ on $P$ by $Y$-automorphisms ($0$ acting as $\mathrm{id}_P$, $(m+n)+\cdot=(m+\cdot)\circ(n+\cdot)$) such that the morphism $\coprod_{m\in M}P\to P\times_YP$ [def-pc-fibre-product] whose restriction to the $m$-th summand is $(m+\cdot,\mathrm{id}_P)$ is an isomorphism. For a $Y$-scheme $P$ let $h_P$ be the sheaf $U\mapsto\operatorname{Mor}_Y(U,P)$ on $Y_{\Et}$ [def-weil-pbc-etale-site]. Let $\underline M$ be the constant sheaf with value $M$ on $Y_{\Et}$ [def-weil-pbc-constant-sheaf], whose sections over $U$ are the locally constant maps $a:|U|\to M$ [lem-weil-pbc-constant-sheaf-sections-locally-constant]; torsors under $\underline M$ are as in [def-sc-gm-torsor] (a sheaf of sets with an action of $\underline M$ which is simply transitive on the sections over every object $U$, and with sections over the members of some covering of every $U$). For an $M$-torsor $P$ over $Y$ let $a\in\underline M(U)$ act on $\varphi\in h_P(U)$ by $(a\cdot\varphi)|_{U_m}=(m+\cdot)\circ\varphi|_{U_m}$ on the open and closed subschemes $U_m=a^{-1}(m)$, $m\in M$. Then:

1. for every $M$-torsor $P$ over $Y$, $h_P$ with this action is a torsor under $\underline M$;
2. every torsor $T$ under $\underline M$ is finite locally constant: there is a covering $\{U_i\to Y\}$ of $Y_{\Et}$ such that $T|_{U_i}$ is isomorphic to the constant sheaf with value $M$ on $(U_i)_{\Et}$ for every $i$;
3. if $T$ is a torsor under $\underline M$ whose underlying sheaf of sets is isomorphic to $h_Q$ for a finite etale morphism $Q\to Y$, then there is an action of $M$ on $Q$ by $Y$-automorphisms making $Q\to Y$ an $M$-torsor over $Y$ such that $h_Q$ with the action of (1) is isomorphic to $T$ as a torsor under $\underline M$ (by an isomorphism of sheaves commuting with the actions).
